{"title":"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is a triangle: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e7a17a6be86d07699b71c5a8a021e5459e93e67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(0,0), B=(36,15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"182\" height=\"18\" /> and both the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are integers. What is the minimum area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> can have?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e05fdc2c464f05890bd047e043065a5705a6386b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{13}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{there is no minimum}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"511\" height=\"37\" /> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> have coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e148d95e9a2349eff0d0ccd1ec50ace5fa25269b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p, q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Then by the Shoelace Formula, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/0/eb0ffdd0972502926a0c5082645b5a3dec74e519.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2} \\lvert {12q-5p} \\rvert$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19d63048b684e6ae23a4bf922d0dffb29f829ff1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert {12q-5p} \\rvert$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> is a positive integer, and by Bezout's Lemma, it can equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (e.g. with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/790e14cbd8ef6c91bf8b28ee0eaaba2bb8a6075b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 2, p = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />), so the minimum area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408e7807deb9da0a3e6f7e263901b96e9f0bd364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2} \\times 1 = \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"80\" height=\"37\" />, which is answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> have coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e148d95e9a2349eff0d0ccd1ec50ace5fa25269b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p, q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f509fdaeb6a8425b004737c3ae0fff2226896905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(36-0)^2+(15-0)^2}=39.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"231\" height=\"35\" /> The equation of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17a5fd8904b672d2584e5a1440c36726dae4233a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x-12y=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" /> Then, by the point-line distance formula the length of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1d75d438b99cfccc53e419a67a0335866a0c5c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{|5p-12q|}{\\sqrt{5^2+12^2}}=\\frac{|5p-12q|}{13}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"196\" height=\"45\" /> Thus the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0ed60b53a75d5260e2b6ec38d2d421141639119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39 \\cdot \\frac{|5p-12q|}{13}=\\frac{3}{2} \\lvert {12q-5p} \\rvert.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"235\" height=\"40\" /> Then proceed as in solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from here.\n</p><p>-AndrewZhong2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME\" title=\"1987 AHSME\">1987 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1987 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1987\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=198